File: openOODA/STATUS.oot
Status: open — 2026-08-25 floor snapshot; rerun the cited audits for current numbers.

---

## 1. TL;DR

The x86 backend is not a usable product floor: 45.3% of COMPILED fixtures silently miscompile via a no-op main and 92.6% of the SSA path is ASM-FAIL (`audit/x86-hostile-probe-v2.oot:73, 158`). The AArch64 backend is shallower on every axis (10 files, 1,388 lines, zero per-shape matchers, no SSA path, 0/3 contract coverage on 14 of 16 features) but fail-closed rather than fail-open (`audit/aarch64-deep-dive.oot:73`, `audit/aarch64-contract-coverage.oot:46`). The path forward is the 5-phase AST pipeline in RFC 0011: replace the 22-template token-matcher ladder with a typed-AST → SSA → x86_64 AT&T emit, gated by typed diagnostics and a per-block register remap.

## 2. x86 backend state

- **Status: FAIL.** 5,750 / 6,936 (82.9%) fixtures COMPILED on emit-x86; 1,185 REFUSED; 1 ASM-FAIL (`audit/x86-hostile-probe-v2.oot:33-36`).
- **Silent-miscompile rate: 45.3%.** 2,607 / 5,750 COMPILED binaries exit 0 with empty stdout; 99.5% of them are a no-op main that `push %rbp / sub $64,%rsp / add $64,%rsp / syscall` (`audit/x86-hostile-probe-v2.oot:59, 75-88`).
- **SSA path is broken.** emit-x86-ssa: 6,426 / 6,936 (92.6%) ASM-FAIL via duplicate labels and undefined forward block references; v1 was 0.2% ASM-FAIL (`audit/x86-hostile-probe-v2.oot:44-51`).
- **Top 5 hostile shapes (empty / total, when present).** Float 158/160 (98.7%), 3-arm match 27/30 (90.0%), Result[T] 179/216 (82.8%), struct 224/277 (80.8%), List[T] 162/202 (80.1%) (`audit/x86-hostile-probe-v2.oot:98-102`).
- **Next 3 fixes (ranked).** (1) make x86_emit.oo refuse on the 5 hostile shapes instead of emitting a no-op main — drops empty-stdout to ~10%; (2) fix the SSA per-block remap — restores SSA from 7.3% to ~95% COMPILED; (3) add a `_start` wrapper that prints "no-output" when main returns without a write — turns silent failures into visible ones (`audit/x86-hostile-probe-v2.oot:148-154`).

## 3. AArch64 backend state

- **10 oodac files, 1,388 lines** — 4.2× fewer files and 4.8× fewer lines than x86 (`audit/aarch64-deep-dive.oot:23, 66`).
- **Zero per-shape matcher files** — x86 has 22; aarch64 has 0; the central `a64_collect_prints` in aarch64_emit.oo:19-124 is a 105-line function with 12 mutable state vars (`audit/aarch64-deep-dive.oot:42, 68`).
- **No SSA path** — `grep -r 'aarch64_ssa' oodac/` returns 0 hits; std codegen is wired but the text-output path is parallel (`audit/aarch64-deep-dive.oot:69-70`).
- **Contract coverage: 14 / 16 features at 0/3.** Only `fn decl` (1/3) and `if` (1/3) have any cell as Y; aarch64 is worse than x86 on 10 of 16 features, same on 5, better-with-asterisk on 1 (`audit/aarch64-contract-coverage.oot:46, 107`).
- **Fail-closed posture.** Unknown shapes set `leftover = true` and exit 1 at aarch64_emit.oo:121; x86's x86_emit_walk.oo:28-30 fail-opens for `KW_WHILE` / `KW_FOR` and emits anyway. 54 aarch64_*.oo fixtures are misfiled in `ooda/fixtures/` instead of `ooda/fixtures-aarch64/` (`audit/aarch64-deep-dive.oot:73, 90, 58`).

## 4. Top 5 critical bugs

1. **No-op main fires for 5 hostile shapes** — 2,607 / 5,750 (45.3%) binaries exit 0 with empty stdout because `x86_emit.oo:90` writes 0 instructions into main (`audit/x86-hostile-probe-v2.oot:90`).
2. **SSA per-block remap generates duplicate / undefined block labels** — 6,426 / 6,936 (92.6%) ASM-FAIL on emit-x86-ssa; `.Lmain_block2` referenced but never emitted, `.Lxss_pi_*` defined twice; bug in `x86_ssa_emit.oo:50-51` (`audit/x86-hostile-probe-v2.oot:50-51`).
3. **Float literals silently miscompile** — 158 / 160 fixtures with Float usage (98.7%) emit the hardcoded `x*y+1.0` body; shape is `x86_emit_float.oo:91` (`audit/x86-hostile-probe-v2.oot:98`).
4. **struct field/type silently miscompile** — 224 / 277 fixtures (80.8%) emit a no-op main when the source uses a struct; bug in `x86_emit_struct.oo:185-202` producing `$c` / `$-` for non-int fields (`audit/x86-hostile-probe-v2.oot:101`, `audit/aarch64-deep-dive.oot:79`).
5. **List[T] silent miscompile on x86** — 162 / 202 fixtures (80.1%) emit a no-op main; hardcoded 20-iteration push-100..119 body in `x86_emit_list.oo:29` (`audit/x86-hostile-probe-v2.oot:102`).

## 5. Top 5 recent wins

1. **Compiler floor pinned at v0.211.0** — `oodac check oodac/main.oo` OK; RAM-cold ~164s, disk-warm ~0.02s for 179 modules (`SHIPPED.oot:15`).
2. **LLVM hello works on the current host** — emit-llvm + clang + run; Result `match` prints `ok`, two-module import prints `2`; lock `scripts/open30_llvm_lock_smoke.oo` (`SHIPPED.oot:45`).
3. **AArch64 backend structural deep-dive audit shipped** — 10 files, 1,388 lines verified; zero SSA confirmed; 54 misfiled fixtures surfaced; lock `audit/aarch64-deep-dive.oot` (`SHIPPED.oot:52`).
4. **x86 emit dispatch dead-arms audit shipped** — 24 token-walker arms inventoried in `x86_emit.oo:73-196`; arm 18 (`x86_match_list_test`) is a broken-emit stub; lock `audit/x86-dead-arms.oot` (`SHIPPED.oot:53`).
5. **x86 std/arch_x86/ call-graph surface map shipped** — 95 files, 3,326 lines, 255 public decls; zero `import "std/arch_x86/"` from oodac/; `elf64_build_executable` at `x86_elf.oo:39-55` returns only 48 bytes and ignores `text_bytes`; lock `audit/x86-std-surface.oot` (`SHIPPED.oot:54`).

## 6. Rebuild blocker

Pure multi-module oodac rebuild cannot complete: Gate 1 (host `check` of `ooda/oodac/main.oo`) trips on `RefinementTypeViolation: token count exceeds 1000` because the host seed binary was built before `tc_refine.oo:22` was raised to 1048576; Gate 2 (the C compile of the stitched all.c) trips on `conflicting types for 'OoL_<Name>'` because `c_emit_olist.oo:25` and `c_emit_struct.oo:104` both emit a real `typedef struct <Name> { ... } <Name>;` for the same name (`audit/rebuild-blocker.oot:11-13, 28-42`). `PURE_SKIP_CHECK=1` at `ooda/bootstrap/oodac_pure_build:113` clears Gate 1 only; no env flag clears Gate 2. The smallest correct fix is an `OO_HAVE_<Name>` ifndef guard in `c_emit_olist.oo:25` plus a tightened stitcher regex in `ooda/bootstrap/oodac_pure_build:305-313` — the c_emit lane owns the file and sign-off is required (`audit/rebuild-blocker.oot:74`).

## 7. Path forward

The 5-phase AST pipeline in RFC 0011 replaces the 22-template token-matcher ladder with a typed-AST → SSA → x86_64 AT&T emit:

1. **Phase A — Foundation.** Replace `x86_emit_stream` with a typed-AST path that calls `ast_parse.oo` + `tc_drive.oo` and lowers to SSA via `x86_ssa_compile.oo`; add a real SSA Call opcode and SysV arg lowerer; wire `ssa_mem2reg.oo` + `ssa_opt.oo`; fix the per-block register remap (the 6,426 ASM-FAIL from bug #2) (`rfcs/0011-x86-ast-pipeline.oot:25-27`).
2. **Phase B — Types.** String-table pass with `.rodata` + `lea`; real struct emitter with field-offset layout; real `List[T]` with bounds-checked `list_new` / `list_push` / `list_get` / `list_set`; real IEEE-754 Float lowering; real `match` lowering to jump tables; DWARF5 debug info (`rfcs/0011-x86-ast-pipeline.oot:27`).
3. **Phase C — Capabilities, contracts, multi-file.** Capability tokens and SECRET taint at emit (mirror `c_emit_secret_*.oo`); multi-file emit (one `.s` per file, `.globl` externs, `as`+`ld` glue); `requires` / `ensures` / `spec` / `verify` via `smt_contract_parse.oo` + `smt_prover_lia.oo` (`rfcs/0011-x86-ast-pipeline.oot:28`).
4. **Phase D — Production glue.** Replace the `x86_emit_direct_elf_binary` `sh`+`printf` shim with a pure in-process ELF64 writer; typed error reporter using `diag_json.oo` shape; x86 runtime registry `oo_x86_alloc` / `oo_x86_list_*` / `oo_x86_str_*` / `oo_x86_arc_*`; bit-identical reproducibility (sorted `.rodata`, deterministic symbol table) (`rfcs/0011-x86-ast-pipeline.oot:29`).
5. **Phase E — Perf + docs + surface.** Inlining (call site < threshold), CSE, LICM, strength reduction; convert every `x86_*.oo` fixture and `x86_*_smoke.oo` to AST-based regression; Academy headers on all 30+ x86 files; move SHIPPED.oot from "lock per template" to "lock per language feature" (`rfcs/0011-x86-ast-pipeline.oot:30`).

The 22 staged rows in `openOODA/ROADMAP.oot` §5.1 each name one smoke that locks the row; RFC 0011 closes when all 22 rows are checked and the smokes pass. The current cycle is in Turn 2 of the AArch64 plan (`audit/aarch64-deep-dive.oot` §5) and sub-turns 2a-2d of the x86 plan (`rfcs/0014-turn2-plan.oot` §2-5).
